Caring for crops means repeated clicks: select a pot, choose a chore from its menu, then repeat for the next pot. Replanting adds more steps after each harvest.

Greenline automates this chain with Tend All, Auto-replant, and optional Auto-fertilize, and it helps the Farming GR-3 robot keep your pots planted. You spend less time clicking through menus and walking between pots, while Stamina, seed, and fertilizer costs stay the same. Features unlock as your Planting level grows, at the levels the game uses for its own farming tools.

[size=5]Main features[/size]
[list]
[*][b]Pot grid.[/b] See every pot by floor and area (Interior, Sunroom, Terrace, Cold Storage, Basement), including empty pots, with crop countdowns and markers for mature crops and problems. Each line shows the light and the temperature of its area, as the HUD does, so you see which pots a cold wave hits. Pin the list to keep it open. From Planting level 2.[/*]
[*][b]Pot details.[/b] Point at a grid cell or a pot in the game world to see crop details in a card pinned next to it. Click a cell to open the pot's menu and move the camera there.[/*]
[*][b]Tend All.[/b] Queue pot chores with one click from Planting level 3, using the game's Stamina costs and limits. Your character tends the pots in the order of the shortest walk around walls and furniture: the current floor first, then the other floors. It replaces the game's own Tend Garden (game 1.1.19611).[/*]
[*][b]Auto-replant.[/b] After "Tend All" harvests a pot, it plants the same crop again. Seeds from a harvest earlier in the same run count. It is on by default. Turn it off with the checkbox below the pot grid. To skip one pot, untick its Auto-replant checkbox in the planting window or the pot's View window.[/*]
[*][b]Auto-fertilize.[/b] Turn it on for a pot, and each replant adds the fertilizer with the largest speed bonus, also when you have less than a full dose. For example, 1 Premium Organic Fertilizer in a pot of size 2 (+50%) beats 2 Basic Fertilizer (+30%).[/*]
[*][b]Replant help.[/b] If replanting cannot proceed, the "Tend All" stops on planting window with a short line showing the pot's last crop and the reason.[/*]
[*][b]Farming Robot GR-3.[/b] Adds a "Same as last crop" mode to its Sowing Presets: the robot replants each pot with its last crop. The robot also tills and plants a pot it harvested before its next harvest (you can turn both off in the config file).[/*]
[*][b]English and Chinese.[/b][/*]
[/list]

Greenline stores the Auto-replant checkbox, and each pot's last crop, Auto-replant setting, and Auto-fertilize setting in the save. The game ignores these values without Greenline, so you can still load the save after removing the mod. A Farming GR-3 set to Same as last crop then plants nothing in that pot size until you pick a seed.

[size=5]You may also like[/size]
If you like Greenline, try [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/survivallog/mods/15]Trapline[/url] for one-click trap collection and a compact trap grid.

[size=5]Requirements[/size]
[list]
[*]Survival Log version 1.1.19611 or later.[/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/survivallog/mods/12]BepInEx for Survival Log[/url]. Install it first.[/*]
[/list]

[size=5]Installation[/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/survivallog/mods/12]BepInEx[/url] [i](if no other mods were installed before, start the game once so BepInEx finishes setup, then quit)[/i].[/*]
[*]Extract this mod's zip into the game folder (the folder with the game .exe). The DLL lands in BepInEx\plugins. Full path example:
[code]C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\Survival Log\BepInEx\plugins\Greenline.dll[/code][/*][/list]

[size=5]Uninstall[/size]
Delete [font=Courier New]Greenline.dll[/font] from the [font=Courier New]BepInEx\plugins[/font] folder.

[size=5]Configuration[/size]
To change mod settings, edit [font=Courier New]BepInEx\config\com.ivmakk.survivallog.greenline.cfg[/font] while the game is closed (see [url=https://github.com/ivmakk-sl/sl-greenline/blob/main/CONFIG.md]CONFIG.md[/url] for every setting). Changes apply at the next game start.

There you can turn off Tend All, the pot tooltips in the game world, and the Farming GR-3 features.

